{"id":"0504536c-10b1-42b0-aa0b-c8509a191816","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"1dd11584a6dd6476","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/git-panel.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"44550ee88e47fac385113c37fa7727e0c4932870","start":31,"end":98},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","GitFileChange","}","from","\"","@brianjenkins94/editor-api/git","\""]},"context":{"after":"a4eb2d27eddc588a"}},"payload":{"text":"Git review panel — a GitHub-Desktop-style changed-files + diff + commit surface, rendered in the SHELL's RHS chrome\n(not the vscode SCM viewlet). Built on Web Awesome components (wa-checkbox / wa-textarea / wa-button / wa-badge) and\nutility classes in a preact tree; what's left in theme/styles/git-panel is the rows' hover/current states and\nthe side-by-side diff renderer's grid. It's a pure hub consumer: it calls\n`git.status` / `git.review` / `git.commit` / `git.discard` (served by git-service.ts and git-review.ts in the workbench realm) over the\nshell hub, and refreshes on `git.changed`. What a pick of lines commits or discards is the service's (shared/git-hunks.ts),\nas it is for an agent's `git_commit` / `git_discard` by hunk: the panel only says which rows. No monaco, no zen-fs here — the \"novel review UI over the engine\" the git-engine\ndecoupling was for. The diff opens in a shell-owned overlay the codehike island mounts into (overlay.body).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:50:34.696Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:50:34.696Z"}
{"id":"0f667e9a-53f8-4c1d-a23f-5ee1204ad734","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"48fb38c7246566c0","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/git-panel.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"c634d6f4ac27976eb526f7aee7350839dbba2ee6","start":16332,"end":16436},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","refreshLater","=","(",")",":","void","=>","{","refresh","(",")",".","catch","(","(",")","=>","{","}",")",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"fbd9280c537b8bc5","after":"015f7164e50bf6c8"}},"payload":{"text":"A refresh nobody waits on: if the workbench is too busy to answer (a large repository loading), the list stays as\nit was until the next `git.changed`, rather than the timeout going up as an uncaught error.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:48:08.644Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:48:08.644Z"}
{"id":"1624e02f-afc2-4784-8ceb-ae7a22d868b6","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"d95f260665c202b9","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/git-panel.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"495d677714af1c2deeda3c87aade56347832f3ac","start":11050,"end":11089},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","problems","=","useChangeProblems","(","hub",")"]},"context":{"before":"924a0dd7471a39fd","after":"e1a646a25e64a6c4"}},"payload":{"text":"(what the change made and fixed in each file: change-problems.tsx)","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:48:59.149Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:48:59.149Z"}
{"id":"1abd46b6-a25f-42d5-a3e8-a2b89ba185b3","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"b218d21d91470908","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/git-panel.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"ba0a3e33da6c670a81f5a8ac2b64a5b65430b40a","start":1699,"end":1720},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","\"","theme/chrome","\""]},"context":{"before":"a50f3ec34f84783d","after":"0d49b12629424440"}},"payload":{"text":"The theme (Web Awesome's layer order among it) first, so git-panel.css's `@layer app` is declared after it (the shell\nimports this module before it imports the theme itself).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:50:28.232Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:50:28.232Z"}
{"id":"208c216b-0b33-4580-b227-be41060ebbeb","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"91748e48b3a26084","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/git-panel.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"c2160aeff48650f2798f6a2cf5050aba60a4b362","start":12804,"end":13249},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","renderPlain","=","(","head",":","string",",","working",":","string",",","rows",":","DiffRowInfo","[]",")",":","void","=>","{","const","diff","=","document",".","createElement","(","\"","div","\"",")",";","diff",".","className","=","\"","sxs-plain","\"",";","for","(","const","row","of","collapse","(","plainRows","(","head",",","working",",","rows",")",")",")","{","const","line","=","document",".","createElement","(","\"","div","\"",")",";","line",".","className","=","\"","sxs-plain-row ","\"","+","row",".","t",";","line",".","textContent","=","ROW_MARKS","[","row",".","t","]","+","row",".","text",";","diff",".","appendChild","(","line",")",";","}","overlay",".","body",".","replaceChildren","(","diff",")",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"d52978208d6193d1","after":"f59d68f6baad4ad7"}},"payload":{"text":"Plain unified diff (fallback when the codehike island can't load — e.g. offline: shiki fetches grammars).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:48:33.886Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:48:33.886Z"}
{"id":"225f2dae-a492-494f-873e-449d869eeaa9","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"7e6227bd52df3347#2","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/git-panel.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"f14bc7557f6e5cadbc6392a4bc3f96e20fe53bc2","start":16654,"end":16663},"shape":{"type":"Identifier","atoms":["useEffect"]},"context":{"before":"48fb38c7246566c0","after":"2043dc8c38560c95"}},"payload":{"text":"Mount-once wiring: the overlay close button, git.changed refresh, and the initial load.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:48:02.421Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:48:02.421Z"}
{"id":"232b05a6-a0b2-49b3-b690-d1bcd3fca794","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"305f9f5edacee4d3","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/git-panel.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"c217677fe24cd39aac97561ca7dd9002a208fc32","start":5132,"end":5203},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","CHUNK_INFO","=","\"","gp-chunk-info wa-font-size-2xs wa-color-text-quiet","\""]},"context":{"before":"1d79441b4255a941","after":"5aa7eda928240e8c"}},"payload":{"text":"A chunk timeline's note line (a status, or the summary above the chunks).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:49:36.943Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:49:36.943Z"}
{"id":"2d69bb37-06af-46c4-bb42-5976ef93463d","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"16ccdc188343bfe3","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/git-panel.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"91df7ca15944bdf28c40684a14dcb49770745858","start":11237,"end":11309},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","[","expanded",",","setExpanded","]","=","useState","<","ReadonlySet","<","string",">",">","(","new","Set","(",")",")"]},"context":{"before":"e1a646a25e64a6c4","after":"be918a9ec07182bc"}},"payload":{"text":"(the files whose edits since the last commit are shown, under their row)","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:48:52.893Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:48:52.893Z"}
{"id":"2f7406e7-e469-49ba-83e9-cd7915ae0863","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"779ede8b6b245041","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/git-panel.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"e432d97b92b6580d233e382d5b4b76aa3dd32d9d","start":16882,"end":17134},"shape":{"type":"UnaryExpression","atoms":["void","(","async","(",")","=>","{","for","(","let","attempt","=","0",";","attempt","<","20",";","attempt","+=","1",")","{","try","{","await","refresh","(","{","\"","timeoutMs","\"",":","1500","}",")",";","return",";","}","catch","{","await","new","Promise","(","(","resolve",")","=>","{","setTimeout","(","resolve",",","500",")",";","}",")",";","}","}","}",")","(",")"]},"context":{"before":"324ffc9f7e3ef1a2","after":"3d26dcbf4e68511b"}},"payload":{"text":"The workbench git service registers late in its boot (and the shell→app→workbench link takes a moment to\nform), so the initial load POLLS with a short timeout until the responder answers — instead of one\ndefault 15s \"no responder\" hang. Once up, `git.changed` drives subsequent refreshes.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:47:49.909Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:47:49.909Z"}
{"id":"37748ef1-0cf8-40b0-be88-bbb2a21b9640","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"41805309406b22b8","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/git-panel.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"cff5fd1eb98d6cc79b7735b51d0e53de9681bac1","start":4554,"end":4646},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","prefersDark","=","(",")",":","boolean","=>","window",".","matchMedia","(","\"","(prefers-color-scheme: dark)","\"",")",".","matches"]},"context":{"before":"4c34c9d2fa3a9bdd","after":"c2aa3fd4dcdd7a7d"}},"payload":{"text":"Current OS colour scheme — the diff highlights with the matching shiki theme (the shell drives the same query).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:49:56.483Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:49:56.483Z"}
{"id":"65a603c0-70bc-46b0-b166-1e05f9e8b634","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"a3b618f11acb28d0#1","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/git-panel.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"2a8d4e40a36ff90237c0df2ae3b1f1bbc653f279","start":14092,"end":14095},"shape":{"type":"Keyword","atoms":["try"]},"context":{"before":"cd0bedbd82a0a73e","after":"c3dc713da9eb64c1"}},"payload":{"text":"Lazy-load the codehike island (react + codehike + shiki) on first diff; fall back to the plain diff if it\ncan't load. Once codehike owns overlay.body (a React root), never touch it with innerHTML again.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:48:15.011Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:48:15.011Z"}
{"id":"6fb5f602-2eda-4e20-bbe6-6b4635c0ca71","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"7a548468700c1985","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/git-panel.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"683a9ef22c13717d2399dc59f5f9d90954b991fd","start":11556,"end":11608},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","deselected","=","useRef","(","new","Set","<","string",">","(",")",")",".","current"]},"context":{"before":"bf1ff41b0079d0c6","after":"3256452fd9524c9c"}},"payload":{"text":"Files fully UN-checked (excluded from the commit). Absence = selected. Per-file PARTIAL line selections + the\nchanged-row count per file live alongside. Mutable refs (mirroring the original imperative model) + force().","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:48:46.545Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:48:46.545Z"}
{"id":"78469a9a-4a59-4002-95ec-eb3c3963c06e","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"c2aa3fd4dcdd7a7d","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/git-panel.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"24dca7302ed20d970533c5b5594171372d31c18c","start":4768,"end":4901},"shape":{"type":"InterfaceDeclaration","atoms":["interface","EditGroup","{","\"","label","\"",":","string",";","\"","kind","\"",":","string",";","\"","startLine","\"",":","number",";","\"","endLine","\"",":","number",";","\"","edits","\"",":","number",";","\"","nodeIds","\"",":","string","[]","}"]},"context":{"before":"41805309406b22b8","after":"1d79441b4255a941"}},"payload":{"text":"A node-grouped chunk of your edits (workbench/edit-history.ts), as `history.chunks` answers it.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:49:49.962Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:49:49.962Z"}
